WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.160
Sometimes, dealing with anomalies that could
destroy the world with a flick of their wrist

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:05.760
can get a little old.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.920
Sure, it definitely wouldn’t be a good thing
if the Devourer of Worlds...Well, devoured

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:15.840
the world, or if SCP-001 - When Day Breaks
- turned us all into weird, melty zombies.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:20.720
But it’s almost impossible to conceive the
sheer scale of destruction that an XK-Class

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.960
End of the World Scenario would cause.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.560
You’d be almost numb to it, if you even
survived.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:32.720
In the words of SCP-2430 creator Josef Stalin,
“The death of one man is a tragedy.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.440
The death of millions is a statistic.”

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.600
Okay, he didn’t actually say that, but it’s
an appropriate quote either way.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.360
Today, we’re talking about a much smaller,
pettier kind of evil.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:48.800
Sure, this anomaly can kill people - and has,
many, many times, in fact - but where it really

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.680
gets its kicks, is in making you feel like
crap on a more emotional level.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:01:00.720
It’s SCP-056: Ironically known by the nickname,
“A Beautiful Person”, because on the inside,

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:04.240
this self-obsessed monster is anything but
beautiful.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:08.240
This crafty creature spent what potentially
could have been hundreds of years around humans

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:13.600
before the SCP Foundation eventually located
and apprehended it, meaning you may have even

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:17.920
run into it at some point or another before
it was rightfully imprisoned.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:21.040
How do you know if you had a brush with SCP-056?

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:25.360
Well, it’s difficult to know for sure, but
perhaps the biggest indicator is that it probably

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.280
annoyed the living hell out of you.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:33.200
You see, SCP-056 is a sentient shapeshifter
with a subtle mind-warping ability, whose

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.840
entire reason for existence is using those
abilities to make everyone around them feel

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:39.520
incredibly inadequate.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:45.360
They don’t have any kind of consistent or
“true” form, only a consistent ethos - And

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:50.160
that ethos is “Anything you can do, I can
do better.”

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.800
And we mean this in its most literal sense.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.800
Whenever SCP-056 is left with a person, an
animal, or even an object, the second all

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:03.120
eyes are taken off of it, it’ll become a
slightly better version of whatever it’s

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:04.000
encountering.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.960
If the thing in question is capable of thinking
or feeling, it will not feel good about this

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:09.920
development.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:14.400
Just like we said, it’s probably not going
to bring the world to its knees, but it sure

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.840
would suck to know SCP-056.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:23.120
Its lack of a consistent form makes SCP-056
a little difficult to think about visually

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.240
- Which was also the reason it was so hard
to catch - but for the sake of consistency,

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:33.360
we’ll present it here with one of its favorite
forms: A woman who’s a real dead ringer

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.160
for “perfection” - famous actress Scarlett
Johanssen, of Black Widow fame.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:48.160
So what is it really like to experience SCP-056’s
anomalous effects first-hand?

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:53.120
Well, we’ll take you through a little crash-course
in anomalous insecurity and frustration.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:57.200
Let’s say that this creature, in human form,
is one of your co-workers.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:01.600
When the Foundation discovered it, it was
working in the fashion industry, but who knows

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.600
what job it could have held before then?

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:08.160
If it worked in your office, it was probably
that one irritating coworker who always wore

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:13.360
nicer clothes than you, had a brighter, whiter
smile, and much better hair.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:17.440
While you were thanklessly toiling away on
the reports for the latest financial quarter,

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.960
056 was schmoozing with your boss on golf
lunches, scoring perfect games and promotions

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:25.440
one “hole in one” at a time.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.240
Of course, they tell you about it at the water
cooler.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:32.160
Like everyone who’s feeling inadequate,
maybe you buy yourself a new car.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:36.160
A vintage Cadillac convertible that makes
you look more like a gangster than an office

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:36.800
drone.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:37.440
Awesome!

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.400
That’ll make all those feelings that you’re
not good enough go away.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.440
You even buy yourself a&nbsp;
stylish pair of sunglasses,&nbsp;

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.360
and start cruising around town with the top

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:49.280
down, hoping that everyone sees how cool you
are now.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:53.840
But when you’re stopped at a stop light,
you see something approaching in the lane

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:54.880
next to you.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:58.880
It’s the latest Rolls Royce, in jet black.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:05.120
And who would be behind the wheel but SCP-056,
in Armani shades that are much nicer than

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:05.840
yours.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:10.880
It grins and nods to you in the mirrors, and
you can feel your soul shriveling up inside

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:14.560
you, only to be replaced by rage and resentment.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.880
Maybe later that month,&nbsp;
you and all your co-workers&nbsp;

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.880
are at a bar, enjoying drinks.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:24.160
Of course, SCP-056 is the best dressed one
there, and is telling all the most interesting

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:24.960
stories.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:30.160
Your jokes don’t get any laughs, but 056
is bringing down the house with every word.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.280
Feeling ignored, you decide to get everyone
a round on you.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:38.880
056 is a designated driver in its new Rolls
Royce, so you just decide to get them a Pepsi

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:39.600
instead.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.160
However, by the time you return to their stool,
they’re nowhere to be seen.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:49.440
A tall glass of Coca Cola with ice cubes is
sitting on the bar next to their seat.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.360
Perhaps one day you finally snap and decide
you can’t take it anymore.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:59.280
You’ll meet SCP-056 after work and put this
showboating jerk in its place at long last.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:03.440
You sneak up on it in an alley with a knife
in your palm and swing for it, but your blade

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.960
never makes contact.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:10.320
SCP-056 unleashes some high-level Jiu-Jitsu
move on you, easily knocks the knife from

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.640
your hands, and beats the living hell out
of you.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:16.880
When you’re later convicted of attempted
murder, all you can do is scream “They made

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:17.840
me do it!”

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:21.120
Again and again in your prison cell.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.760
Envy can do crazy things to a person.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.840
But there’s more!

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:30.800
Really, if you lose your mind from an encounter
with SCP-056, you still haven’t done too

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:31.600
badly.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:38.000
While its methods of attack are more commonly
psychological, as we alluded to earlier, SCP-056

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:42.400
is definitely not above committing some pretty
horrifying acts of violence.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:47.600
SCP-056 was discovered in its clothing design
job after causing an unusually high number

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:51.760
of murders, suicides, and mental breakdowns
among its coworkers.

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:56.560
However, things took an even more unpleasant
turn when the Foundation sent personnel to

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:57.440
detain it.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:03.360
SCP-056 reacted poorly to this show of potential
force, and turned into something even more

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:07.040
dangerous than the Foundation planned for
in getting it under control.

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:11.920
We don’t know exactly what it transformed
into due to SCP Foundation redactions, but

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:14.320
our guesses for what it transformed into would&nbsp;

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:17.600
either be a giant monster,&nbsp;
a Rambo-esque unstoppable

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:21.760
super-soldier, or something like one of those
huge killer robots from Robocop.

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:26.720
Pick your favorite down there in the comments,
but whatever the case, it caused the unfortunate

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:30.240
deaths of seventeen agents and ten civilians.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:34.480
The incident was blamed on an employee at
the company going postal and deciding to kill

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:38.320
a bunch of innocents, which...Technically
wasn’t untrue?

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:44.000
Not long after, Foundation operatives were
able to tranquilize SCP-056.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:48.240
Perhaps you think this nasty little monster
decided to mellow out a little bit after being

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:52.560
contained, but if you did think that, I’m
afraid you’d be dead wrong.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:57.600
It just decided to start terrorizing Foundation
staff with its infuriating anomalous abilities

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:58.560
instead.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.720
Wait until you see this!

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:06.640
Compared to a lot of entities locked up at
the SCP Foundation, SCP-056 really lives in

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:07.920
the lap of luxury.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:12.960
It has a well-furnished room, easy access
to members of staff, and is given permission

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:18.560
to interact with any object it desires - As
long as those objects aren’t anomalous.

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:23.040
Why is this Euclid-Class anomaly with over
seventeen dead Foundation staff members to

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.880
its name given so much leeway?

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:30.400
Well, to answer that, remember the ethos:
“Anything you can do, I can do better.”

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:35.120
And this holds true, whether we’re talking
physical appearance or one’s capacity to

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:37.280
commit tremendous acts of violence.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:42.720
The Foundation is forced to cater to most
of SCP-056’s whims, or it’ll become a

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:46.960
hell of a lot more dangerous in response to
any kind of external resistance.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:47.520
See?

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:51.520
We told you it’d suck to have to know this
thing, and nobody knows that better than the

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:54.080
employees of the SCP Foundation who are forced&nbsp;

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:57.120
to interact with it on a&nbsp;
daily basis for containment

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.160
and testing.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:01.840
First, let’s take a look at some of the
forms it’s occupied since it began its time

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.600
at the SCP Foundation.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:09.520
When a researcher brought in their beloved
pooch, SCP-056 decided to flex on it by becoming

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:12.000
a beautiful, well-groomed labrador retriever.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:16.880
When younger female staff passed it, it decided
to once again take on its Scarlett Johanssen

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:17.440
form.

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:22.160
When speaking to a group of other researchers
about intelligence, it became a female researcher

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:27.280
with an IQ score thirty points higher than
the top-scoring human researcher on site.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:31.600
When it took a trip to the containment site’s
gym, where the guards and mobile task forces

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:36.400
exercise and train, it decided to take its
flexes to a more literal level.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:41.040
It transformed into a ripped, hunky bodybuilder,
who strutted into the middle of the gym and

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:44.400
bench-pressed 250 kilos, no problem.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:48.560
This was thirty kilos more than the strongest
human guard working at the site.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:53.840
Its commitment to being the best is so great
that when left alone in its containment chamber,

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:58.080
it will sometimes literally transform into
a nicer couch than the one the Foundation

00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:59.280
provided for it.

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:01.200
Doesn’t it just make your blood boil?

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.520
But wait, there’s more!

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:07.760
Just in case this wasn’t absurd enough,
the Foundation felt like testing the limits

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:09.600
of its anomalous abilities.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:15.440
In particular, they were extremely eager to
see if 056 had a secret default form.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:19.920
They left it alone with a single security
camera in order to observe what it transformed

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:22.000
into when not being observed.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.680
And can you guess what happened?

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:28.320
It turned into an even higher-quality security
camera, and stared back.

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:33.520
While the transformations can only take place
while 056 isn’t being observed, it’s very

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:37.680
astute at creating periods where it can’t
be seen or interacted with.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:42.160
Vision or camera feeds have been known to
briefly go foggy in order to facilitate a

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:43.200
transformation.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:48.480
It’s fitting that 056, being the ultimate
diva, will only ever let people look at it

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.000
on its own terms.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:54.960
It also seems to get off on causing shame
- and the degree to which that statement is

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:59.040
metaphorical is, well, open to interpretation.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:03.520
Staff members made insecure by its antics
feel compelled to enter its cell and verbally

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:08.880
berate it, at which point 056 will shame them
even harder, and send them out with their

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:10.640
tail between their legs.

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:15.120
It’s like every toxic friend rolled into
one nasty package.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:21.040
Curious as to what else SCP-056 was capable
of, the Foundation conducted a few other tests

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:24.240
between SCP-056 and their personnel.

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:28.800
Here, they discovered that 056 seemed incredibly
responsive to intent.

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:33.920
When a D-Class was sent in with a knife and
the intent to kill, 056 transformed into a

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:37.760
lean, athletic man, before disarming and killing
the D-Class.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:41.600
A somewhat attractive D-Class female was sent
in with a bottle of wine.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:46.640
056 became a beautiful woman and accepted
the wine, before taking a sip, and spitting

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:49.040
it back into the D-Class’ face.

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:53.120
A mixed-gender pair of D-Classes were sent
in next with no real intent.

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:58.080
056 became an attractive woman in a well-tailored
business suit, who looked over the pair before

00:10:58.080 --> 00:10:59.600
kicking them both out.

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:02.240
Ten male D-Classes were sent in after that.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:07.280
056 turned into a beautiful woman in a low-cut
dress, and simply waited until the ten men

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:12.240
were driven mad with desire and began physically
fighting one another for her affection.

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:16.720
She watched them doing this for seven minutes
before laughing and leaving the simp squadron

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:18.160
to duke it out alone.

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:22.480
In another test, a female staff member with
Level 4 clearance, who was also judged to

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:27.600
be the most attractive woman on site - which
seems like an HR issue that the Ethics Committee

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:31.840
should probably look into - was sent into
056’s testing chamber.

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:38.320
056 became, quote, “An extremely aesthetically
pleasing woman, who displayed a large lexicon

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:40.800
and understanding of management skills.”

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:41.520
Unquote.

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:46.160
The two spoke for around 90 minutes until
the Level 4 staff member stormed out in a

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:47.040
rage.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:52.080
Recently, 056 has requested access to the
internet, saying that the Foundation has been

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:56.240
unable to provide it with enough sycophants,
and that via the internet, the whole world

00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:58.480
will be able to see its face.

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:04.560
If ever 056 got onto YouTube and transformed
into a more successful SCP Channel, I just

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:06.720
don’t think we’d be able to take it!

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:09.200
Thankfully, this request was denied.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:15.960
Now go check out “SCP Minecraft World Destroyer
SCP-4335 - A Welt In The Crucible” and “SCP-2430

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:21.600
- Immortal Hitler Clone” for more anomalies
you really just wanna punch in the face!

